-- converse.attested_language_batch(ids[]) -> (id, lang): the primary language of EACH id,
-- in one pass. This is the canonical body; converse.attested_language(one) delegates here.
--
-- WHY IT EXISTS (§15). This argmax was written twice: once as the scalar
-- converse.attested_language, and once inline as taxonomy.bubble_up's `cand_lang` CTE --
-- identical predicate, identical GROUP BY, identical tie-break, two bodies free to
-- drift. bubble_up then ran BOTH per call: the scalar once for the term, the inline
-- copy once for the candidate set.
--
-- WHY IT IS A BATCH. One batched probe covers every id at once; laplace.attestations
-- is HASH (subject_id), so each id resolves inside its own leaf. A per-term loop
-- would pay one statement per token. Under auto_explain on
-- compose_batch, the per-token form showed cand_lang at 32,438 ms over 728 loops.
--
-- The definition is unchanged from the scalar: argmax over SUM(sum_score_fp1e9) per
-- Language-typed context, ties on context_id. A row COUNT here would be the
-- frequency prior §7 forbids -- the weight is the fold's own adjudicated input, not
-- a tally. Contexts are not all languages (chess play and ordinals appear there
-- too), so the context entity is type-checked rather than assumed.
--
-- Ids with no Language-typed attestation return NO ROW, not a NULL row. Callers
-- LEFT JOIN and treat the absence as "no primary language", which is the same
-- structural answer the scalar's NULL carried.
-- Preserve function OIDs: atomic callers depend on these unchanged signatures.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION converse.attested_language_batch(p_ids bytea[])
    RETURNS TABLE(id bytea, lang bytea)
    LANGUAGE sql STABLE PARALLEL SAFE
BEGIN ATOMIC
    SELECT DISTINCT ON (a.subject_id) a.subject_id, a.context_id
    FROM laplace.attestations a
    WHERE a.subject_id = ANY (p_ids)
      AND laplace.is_language(a.context_id)
    GROUP BY a.subject_id, a.context_id
    ORDER BY a.subject_id, SUM(a.sum_score_fp1e9) DESC, a.context_id;
END;
